River.; Fluvius.
Fluviatile.; Fluviatilis.

@AC 78. "The river," in the garden (Genesis 2) = wisdom; "the first river" thence = good and truth; "the second," the Knowledge of all things which are of good and truth, or of love and faith, which are of the internal man; "the third" = reason; "the fourth" = knowledge, which is of the external man. All are from wisdom; and this is from love and faith in the Lord. @658[end].

@107. "A river out of Eden" = wisdom from love.

