@315[3]. A hat on the crown of which was a rosary surrounded with small sapphires.

@SE 6110[8]. The commonness, when there is love truly conjugial, is the plane in which the deliciousnesses form themselves from within, as upon the plane of the rose, and each rose becomes a plane, in which are formed interior deliciousnesses to eternity.

