@--[3]. The "ruby," which is in the first place, in the Original Language, is derived from a word which means redness.

@DSS 42. Hence, the Word, in its ultimate bosom, from its natural sense in which are the two interior ones, is like a ruby and a diamond: from celestial flame, like a ruby...

@AR 232. The Divine sphere which encompasses the Lord... appears, in the Celestial Kingdom, glowing red like a ruby...

